{"id":"G5101","lemma":"τίς","transliteration":"tis","sayIt":"tis","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"which?","meaning":"τίς, neut., τί, genitive, τίνος, interrog. pron., [in LXX for מָה ,מִי ;] in masc. and fem.,\nwho, which, what?; in neut., which, what?, used both in direct and in indirect questions.\nI. I. As subst.,\n1. 1. masc., fem.: τίς; who, what?, Mat.3:7 26:68; Mrk.11:28, Luk.9:9, al. mult.; with genitive partit., Act.7:52, Heb.1:5, al; before ἐκ (= genitive partit.), Mat.6:27, Luk.14:28, Jhn.8:46; = ποῖος, Mrk.4:41 6:2, Luk.19:3, Act.17:19, al.; = πότερος (M, Pr., 77), Mat.21:31 27:17, Luk.22:27, al.; = ὅς or ὅστις (rare in cl.; cf. Bl., §50, 5; M, Pr., 93), Act.13:25.\n2. Neut.: τί; what?, Mat.5:47 11:7, Mrk.10:3, al.; χάριν τίνος, 1Jn.3:12; διὰ τί, Mat.9:11, al.; εἰς τί, Mat.14:31, al.; elliptically, ἵνα τί (sc. γένηται), why, Mat.9:5, al.; τί οὖν, Rom.3:9 6:1, 15 1Co.14:15, al.; τί γάρ, Rom.3:3, Phi 1:18; τί ἐμοὶ (ὑμῖν) καὶ σοί, see: ἔγω.\nII. As adj.: who? what? which?, Mat.5:46, Luk.14:31, Jhn.2:18, al.\nIII. As adv.: = διὰ τι (τί ὅτι), why, Mat.6:28, Mrk.4:40, Luk.6:46, Jhn.18:23, al.; in rhet. questions, = a negation, Mat.27:4, Jhn.21:22, 23 1Co.5:12 7:16, al. in exclamations (like Heb. מָה), how (2Ki.6:20, Psa.3:2, al.), Luk.12:49.\n(AS)","glosses":["what","who","why","which","how","whom"],"count":504,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-3","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"who","kjv":"who"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"how","kjv":"wherewith"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":46,"renderings":{"bsb":"what","kjv":"what"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":47,"renderings":{"bsb":"what","kjv":"what"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"what","kjv":"what"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"what","kjv":"what"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":27,"renderings":{"bsb":"Who","kjv":"hich"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"why","kjv":"why"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"What","kjv":"What"}},{"cha